# Multilevel Inheritance: 
In MLI, a class is inherited from its parent class, and from that parent class, another child class is inherited. forming a chain of inheritance (Grandparent ➔ Parent ➔ Child).

class Grandparent():
  def oldgen(self):
    print("We are your Grandparents")

class Parent(Grandparent):
  def medgen(self):
    print("We are your Parents")

class Child(Parent,Grandparent):
  def newgen(self):
    print("I am your Child")

c = Child()
c.oldgen()
c.medgen()
c.newgen()

